gination platform for commercial, consumer, small business, and mortgage lending, such as the Commercial Loan Origination System that automates the loan lifecycle; Consumer Lending solution, which offers an omnichannel solution with automated credit decisioning and integrations; and Small Business Loan Origination solution for automation and machine learning. In addition, it offers Credit Monitoring, manages credit risks, monitors performance, and uncovers growth opportunities through a data-driven platform; Portfolio Analytics solution, which offers customizable dashboards to track loan, deposit, and application data; and Integration & Intelligence, provides integration capabilities to connect core banking systems, fintech applications, and third-party services via open APIs and a partner marketplace. The company serves global, enterprise, regional, and community banks, credit unions, challenger banks, and independent mortgage banks, business development managers, account executives, field sales engineers, and customer success managers. nCino, Inc. was founded in 2011 and is headquartered in Wilmington, North Carolina.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Sean  Desmond | CEO, President & Director | Age 51 | Compensation: $1.0M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $353K ranks in the below the sector median among Technology peers, with revenue growing 21%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $49K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $44K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["nCino, Inc. is a mid-cap technology business with a $2.1B market cap on $595M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +13% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +6.7pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at -4% against a 12% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 60% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $83M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 14 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 17.39\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 0.2\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 5.8% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and stock-based comp at 12% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 3.2% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 93% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.9270883617267375},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (17.1% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Goodwill represents 65% of total assets \u2014 a large impairment risk hanging over book value","sev":"red","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $2.4M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 8% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Technology ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (43% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"nCino (NASDAQ:NCNO) Stock Price Breaks Below 50-Day Moving Average \u2013 Time to Sell?","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/20/ncino-nasdaqncno-stock-price-breaks-below-50-day-moving-average-time-to-sell.html","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795170179.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.802,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Avoiding Lag: Real-Time Signals in (NCNO) Movement","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/23/Avoiding_Lag:_Real-Time_Signals_in_NCNO_Movement_111226041201_1794517921.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794517921.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.823,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Reviewing Consensus Cloud Solutions (NASDAQ:CCSI) & nCino (NASDAQ:NCNO)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/08/reviewing-consensus-cloud-solutions-nasdaqccsi-ncino-nasdaqncno.html","date":"2026-11-08","timestamp":1794161805.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.949,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"nCino (NASDAQ:NCNO) Insider April Rieger Sells 8,008 Shares of Stock","source":"thelincolnia